.\" dp(1) — manual page for dp, the project dev plan tracker.
.TH DP 1 "2026-09-30" "dp 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dp \- per\-project dev plan, todo and decision tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dp \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dp
tracks plans (milestones), todos, and architecture decisions (ADRs) for a
single project in one SQLite database at
.IR .dp/dp.db .
Like
.BR git (1),
it locates the database by walking up from the current directory, so
commands work from any subdirectory. Run
.B "dp init"
in the project root once, before other commands.
.PP
The database uses WAL journaling, enforced foreign keys and a 5s busy
timeout; schema migrations are applied automatically on startup. Commit
.I .dp/
to version control or add it to
.I .gitignore
as you prefer. Inspect the data directly with
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
If a database exists in the current directory or any parent, print its
path and change nothing. Otherwise create
.I .dp/dp.db
in the current directory and apply migrations. Idempotent.
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Create a new todo.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIID\fR
Attach the todo to plan \fIID\fR (must exist).
.TP
\fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR
Due date, \fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR
Priority; see
.BR PRIORITIES .
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fILIST\fR
Comma\-separated tags; surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
.TP
\fB\-\-detail\fR \fITEXT\fR
New long description, shown by \fBdp show\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B list
Print todos (table by default; see \fB--format\fR)
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIID\fR
Only todos attached to plan \fIID\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-overdue\fR
Only todos whose due date lies in the past; combines with the view flags
below.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Open plus \fIin_progress\fR and \fIblocked\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-done\fR
Only completed todos; takes precedence over \fB\-\-all\fR.
.RE
.TP
.BI "show " ID
Print one todo in full detail.
.TP
.BI "done " ID
Mark a todo as done: sets status to \fIdone\fR and records \fIdone_at\fR.
Idempotent \(em an already\-done todo prints a notice and is left
unchanged. Reopen with \fBdp mod ID \-\-status open\fR, which clears
\fIdone_at\fR.
.TP
.BI "rm " ID
Delete a todo permanently.
.TP
.BI "mod " ID
Change the given fields of a todo; omitted flags leave the field
unchanged. There is no \fB\-\-plan\fR \(em a todo's plan assignment
cannot be changed. With no flags at all, prints \(dqNothing to modify\(dq.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fITEXT\fR
New title.
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fISTATUS\fR
New status; see
.BR STATES .
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR
New priority.
.TP
\fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR
New due date.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fILIST\fR
Replace the tag list.
.RE
.TP
.B plan
Operate on plans (milestones / phases).
.RS
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Create a plan; accepts \fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR,
\fB\-p\fR/\fB\-\-priority\fR and \fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR.
.TP
.B list
Summarize plans with per\-plan open\-task counts.
.TP
.BI "show " ID
Print a plan in detail, its open todos, and how many todos in it are
done.
.TP
.BI "done " ID
Mark a plan as done.
.RE
.TP
.B decision
Operate on decision records (ADRs).
.RS
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Record a decision. \fB\-\-context\fR \fITEXT\fR and \fB\-\-decision\fR
\fITEXT\fR are required; \fB\-\-consequence\fR \fITEXT\fR is optional.
.TP
.B list
List all decisions, accepted ones first.
.TP
.BI "accept " ID
Move a proposed decision to accepted. Refuses if the decision is already
superseded.
.TP
.BI "supersede " "OLD NEW"
Mark OLD as superseded by NEW. NEW must already be accepted; a decision
cannot supersede itself, and only once.
.RE
.TP
.B stats
Print counters: active plans, open / in_progress / blocked / overdue
todos, and todos done today, in the last 7 days, and in total.
.TP
.BI "generate " SHELL
Print a completion script for
.IR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " elvish ", " powershell " or " man
to stdout; redirect it into your shell's completion directory
(e.g.\& ~/.config/fish/completions/dp.fish).
.TP
.BI "help " "[COMMAND]"
Print help for dp or for one subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " FORMAT
Output format for read commands (\fBdp list\fR, \fBdp show\fR, \fBdp stats\fR,
\fBdp plan list/show\fR, \fBdp decision list\fR): \fBtable\fR (default),
\fBjson\fR or \fBmarkdown\fR. May be given before or after the subcommand.
In json mode stdout carries only JSON; empty results print \fB[]\fR.
Write commands ignore this flag and keep human\-readable confirmations.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help; with a subcommand, print its help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH PRIORITIES
\fBhigh\fR/1, \fBmedium\fR/2 and \fBlow\fR/3; names and numbers are
interchangeable, names are case\-insensitive. The default is
\fBmedium\fR.
.SH STATES
Tasks move \fIopen\fR -> \fIin_progress\fR -> \fIdone\fR, with
\fIblocked\fR as a side state. Both \fBdp done\fR and
\fBdp mod \-\-status done\fR record \fIdone_at\fR; moving to any other
status clears it. A todo is overdue when its due date lies in the past
and it is not done.
.PP
Plans move \fIactive\fR -> \fIdone\fR, set only by \fBdp plan done\fR.
.PP
Decisions move \fIproposed\fR -> \fIaccepted\fR -> \fIsuperseded\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dp init
dp plan add "Q4 refactor auth" --due 2026-12-31 -p high
dp add "Implement OAuth login" --plan 1 --due 2026-10-15 -p high -t auth,backend
dp list
dp list --overdue
dp mod 2 --status in_progress
dp done 2
dp plan done 1
dp decision add "Use SQLite" --context "Need zero-config embedded storage" --decision "rusqlite with bundled SQLite" --consequence "Single-file db, easy to back up"
dp decision accept 1
dp decision supersede 1 4
dp stats
dp list --format=markdown
dp stats --format=json | jq .
dp generate fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/dp.fish
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .dp/dp.db
SQLite database for the project, created in the directory where
.B "dp init"
ran. Transient
.I .dp/dp.db\-wal
and
.I .dp/dp.db\-shm
files may sit next to it while dp is running.
.PP
The database is found by walking up from the current directory. With no
database in any parent directory, commands other than
.B init
fail and point at the current directory as the place to run
.BR init .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dp
exits 0 on success (including \-\-help and \-\-version), 1 on runtime
failure with a diagnostic on stderr (database not initialized, unknown
id, invalid date or status, plan referenced by \fBdp add \-\-plan\fR does
not exist), and 2 on usage errors detected by the argument parser.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1), git (1)
